updated: 2026-10-03
changelog: |
  0.1.0: initial kit. The AO-SDLC gates (spec validator, backlog lint, id
  minter, evolve picker, gate-check hook) lifted from bamr87/law-ai (the
  superset) and genericized: every tool takes `--root`, the hook finds tools/
  or scripts/, and law-ai's hard-coded constitution §13 ranking check becomes
  data in an optional specs/_review_questions.json (review-questions.example.json
  reproduces it exactly). Run against law-ai and gitorio, the kit tools give
  output identical to each repo's own copy, and law-ai's
  tests/test_specs_and_backlog.py and tests/test_backlog_picker.py pass with
  the kit copies swapped in.
  archive/ holds byte-exact copies of the pre-kit tools from both repos
  (stamp 0.0.0) so an upgrader can tell an untouched copy from a hand-edited one.
notes: The four tools/*.py files are byte-identity files (UPS-WORK-07). A repo keeps them identical to this kit and puts repo-specific behaviour in specs/_review_questions.json. Templates (spec/plan/tasks, BACKLOG, constitution) are seeded once and then owned by the repo.
